                <head>Methods of warfare: Charges of illegal and inhumane conduct on the part of
                    belligerent forces—Attitude of the United States</head>
                <p>[No attempt is here made to include all the charges and evidence submitted to the
                    Department relative to alleged violations of the Hague regulations of war on
                    land and other agreements designed to reduce the inhumanity and destructiveness
                    of war, nor the demands for protests addressed to it by American citizens. The
                    following selection of documents is designed primarily to set forth the attitude
                    taken by the American Government toward the subject.]</p>






































